From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ss3ds <ss3ds@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ss3ds: wild life round 4: families, dusk and dawn, rain
 species, chases, cave Zubat, quirks, clock-seeded randomness

Alive wild Pokemon: a pair can be a parent with its young (drawn 0.7x, a few levels lower, bouncier). When the time of day changes, land ones that are not in the new table nap or walk off and slip into the grass, and the new ones arrive soon after. In the rain the map's own water Pokemon (Poliwag, Psyduck, Wooper...) sometimes come out onto land. Hunters briefly chase prey close by (Ekans and Rattata, Pidgey and Caterpie, Zangoose and Seviper...); the player always takes priority. Caves get Zubat and Golbat fly-bys from the cave's own table (never in the dark before Flash). The wild random numbers (spots, behaviours) are now mixed with the console clock at boot and on every map entry, so a Continue and the same walk no longer replay the same spawns. Each one gets its own quirk from its spawn (lazy, energetic or watchful pace), unbothered ones often stop to turn and look around, and new ones pop out of tall grass with a rustle or surface with a splash. State magic 'WIL=' (new flags field). Logs: "its young", "time of day changed", "went home", "rain brings", "chases".
